/.phpunit.cache
/node_modules
# /public/build is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# The compiled front-end lives there, and the production server has no npm to
# rebuild it — so if git does not carry it, nothing does. It was ignored until
# 2026-08-30, and every JavaScript change since had to be copied to the server
# by hand; four deploys in a row went out with a stale bundle because that step
# was missed, which looks exactly like a broken feature (a clock printed by PHP
# that never ticks, because the script that ticks it is not there).
#
# Cost of this: `npm run build` rewrites these files with new content hashes, so
# two people building at once conflict in manifest.json. Resolve by taking
# either side and running `npm run build` again — the output is generated, never
# hand-edited, so no work can be lost in that conflict.
#
# /public/hot stays ignored: it is written by `npm run dev` and points at a
# localhost address. Committed, it would send production to a dev server.
/public/hot
/public/image
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
.env
.env.backup
.env.production
